            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="BUR04" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName>Captain</roleName>
                        <forename>James</forename>
                        <surname>Burney</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1750-06-13">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1821-11-17"/>
                    <occupation>naval officer</occupation>
                    <occupation>writer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Burney was a sailor and he travelled with Captain James Cook on his second voyage of discovery in 1772. He later published 
      <title>A Chronological History of the Discoveries in the South Sea or Pacific Ocean</title> , 5 vols. (1803–17) and was 
      elected a fellow of the Royal Society in 1810.  He was 
    a friend of <persName key="LAM01">Charles Lamb</persName>, <persName key="HAZ01">William Hazlitt</persName> 
      and <persName key="ROB03">Henry Crabb Robinson</persName>. </p>
                        <p>Godwin recorded his death.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
